BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Kwaidan — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261107T143000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261107T153000
DTSTAMP:20261108T221058Z
UID:e1ff9730b96d282a8e0f64fd08f8@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Breathtakingly photographed on hand-painted sets\, Kwaidan is 
 at once a Japanese woodcut writ large\, and an abstract wash of luminescen
 t colors that seem to come from another world. An electronic soundtrack by
  avant-garde composer Toru Takemitsu plays hauntingly with natural sounds
 —crickets\, rain\, the cracking of wood\, the loud silence of snow. Yet 
 the stories—four of Lafcadio Hearn’s ghostly tales—strangely contrad
 ict this plastic splendor in their simple\, aching humanity. All are tales
  of mortals caught by forces beyond their comprehension when the supernatu
 ral world intervenes in their lives. This version of Kwaidan is the origin
 al three-hour Director’s Cut.\nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https:
 //events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331140-film-screening-kwaidan
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331140-film-screening-kwaidan
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
