CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:How did South Korea’s rapid economic transformation shape it
 s democracy\, institutions\, and society? In his book\, Keun Lee examines 
 South Korea’s development since 1945 through a framework of compressed d
 evelopment\, decompression\, and convergence. He explores how rapid growth
  helped create a middle class that demanded political freedom\, and how IM
 F-led reforms following the Asian financial crisis reshaped the country’
 s economic trajectory. The seminar will examine the book's findings. Read 
 a full abstract here . About the Speaker Keun Lee is a Distinguished Profe
 ssor of Economics at Chung-Ang University and professor emeritus at Seoul 
 National University. He is a fellow at the Canadian Instit\nCategory: Acad
 emic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/book-seminar-capita
