DESCRIPTION:PUBLIQuartet brings its wide-ranging\, toe-tapping Rhythm Nati
 on to D.C. in a program that reimagines the string quartet through the pul
 se of American music. Newly commissioned works stand alongside music by Da
 niel Bernard Roumain\, Jlin\, Henry Threadgill\, Jeff Scott\, Fodé Lassan
 a Diabaté\, Mazz Swift\, and Eddie Venegas\, drawing on traditions that s
 pan hip hop\, jazz\, Afro-Cuban music\, electronic sound\, and contemporar
 y classical composition. Anchored by tributes to Janet Jackson’s iconic 
 album Rhythm Nation \, the concert connects cultures\, generations\, and a
 rtistic traditions through the ensemble’s adventurous spirit and virtuos
 ic playing. There is an overall 6 ticket limit for this event. Publ\nCateg
 ory: Arts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/publ
 iquartet-rhythmnation
