CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The Torah and the Qur'an tell stories about many of the same f
 igures — above all\, Moses\, the prophet the Qur'an names more often tha
 n any other. For fourteen centuries\, Jews and Muslims have interpreted th
 ese stories through traditions in each other's shadow\, amid rivalry\, exc
 hange and mutual influence. What happens when they are read side by side? 
 Join GW's Ambassador John L. Loeb\, Jr. Institute for Religious Freedom an
 d Democracy for a discussion about what the two scriptures share\, where 
 they diverge and what reading them together can — and cannot — do for 
 Jews and Muslims today. Speakers: Rick Sopher (Woolf Institute) is co-auth
 or (with Abdulla Galadari) of the recently published Illumin\nCategory: Ac
 ademic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/one-moses-two-scr
 iptures-the-torah-and-the-quran-in-conversation
