SUMMARY:Oglethorpe Theatre presents Cyrano De Bergerac — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261120T200000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261120T220000
DTSTAMP:20261108T221058Z
UID:710c53a1525102754cc808ca3b14@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Theater\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:A genius with language\, Cyrano secretly loves the radiant Rox
 ane\, but she loves the beautiful but inarticulate Christian. Convinced of
  his own ugliness\, Cyrano offers to act as a go-between and writes beauti
 ful love letters for Christian to give to Roxane. This verbal deception se
 ts in motion a poignant and often hilarious love triangle in which each ch
 aracter is torn between the lure of physical attraction and the seductive 
 power of words. Martin Crimp’s radical adaptation reimagines the classic
  love story through spoken word\, contemporary poetry and rap—creating a
  world where words are everything.\nCategory: Theater\nOriginal listing: h
 ttps://www.artsatl.org/event/oglethorpe-theatre-presents-cyrano-de-bergera
 c/2026-11-20/
LOCATION:Conant Performing Arts Center at Oglethorpe University\, 4484 Pea
 chtree Rd NE\, Atlanta\, GA\, 30319
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/oglethorpe-theatre-presents-cyrano-de-be
 rgerac/2026-11-20/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
