DESCRIPTION:New work from an award-winning idiot. Join Beth Anne (a woman!
 )\, a middle-aged beauty queen (almost!)\, who has spent her life shape-sh
 ifting into what she thinks others want\, only to realize she doesn’t kn
 ow herself at all. She looks for her reflection in Medusa\, the Sirens of 
 The Odyssey\, and the Weird Sisters of Macbeth. These misunderstood women 
 pull her through the wreckage of her past\, forcing her to confront the st
 ories she’s been told about what it means to be beautiful\, desirable\, 
 good and worthy. In a wild\, theatrical unraveling\, Beth Anne is ripped o
 pen and reborn as something powerful\, ferocious and entirely her own. Wri
 tten and performed by Julia VanderVeen. Directed by Jess Laza\nCategory: T
 heater\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/dentata-julia-vand
 erveen/
